From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thororen <78185467+thororen1234@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:55:16 -0400
Subject: fix: resolve Windows 8+ APIs at runtime for Windows 7

Chromium imports several Windows 8+ functions directly, which prevents
the binary from loading on Windows 7, and CHECKs that ProcessPrng (a
Windows 10 export) exists. Resolve these at runtime instead and fall
back to the Windows 7 equivalent, or to the existing failure path:

* GetSystemTimePreciseAsFileTime -> GetSystemTimeAsFileTime
* QueryUnbiasedInterruptTimePrecise -> QueryUnbiasedInterruptTime
* DiscardVirtualMemory -> the existing MEM_RESET fallback
* PrefetchVirtualMemory, Get/SetProcessInformation,
  Get/SetProcessMitigationPolicy, SetThreadInformation,
  EventSetInformation and the package APIs -> report unsupported
* ProcessPrng -> RtlGenRandom (advapi32!SystemFunction036)

This patch is needed for Windows 7 support and is not suitable for
upstreaming.

